      "writtenOn": "2024-03-14T06:38:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack, thanks for explain.\nNot for this CL.\nDo we want any chicken out flag for that behavior change?\nI\u0027m wondering if there is any case where\napp didn\u0027t expect to see local networks and causes compatibility problems.\ne.g. OEMs which just change targetSdk without testing with any local networks.",
      "parentUuid": "1ab5cd26_85dfb44e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "29ff998bb9ba3a3e380078bf9d789e750748d03f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57a8546a_f95ca47a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-14T06:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, we don\u0027t have flag for this behavior change.  \nI don\u0027t think having flag is helpful for this case.\nIf some apps targeting V expect the behavior of getting callback from local networks, disabling this behavior change will break their apps.\nSince we define compat flags which will be documented, I think we can assume developers take care of behavior changes caused by target sdk bump.",
      "parentUuid": "36f00b17_060637f6",
